<p>
    Software engineering is often more like ethics than like mathematics. 
    There are broad ideas which most software developers agree are good, such as avoiding global variables.
    And there are narrow scenarios in which everyone would agree that one solution is better than another.
    However, real-world problems depend on too many subjective factors
    to be able to definitively say that one solution is the best solution.
</p>
<p>
    Many software development opinions are based on which strategies are easiest for the programmer.
    This, of course, is highly subjective.
</p>
<p>
    The following document contains all my software development opinions.
    I expect that these opinions will change over time, and this document will be frequently updated.
</p>

