<h3>Modules</h3>
<p>
    Good modules are the key to clean code.

A good module has an easy-to-use API that encapsulates a large amount of complexity.
A good module has as few dependencies as possible.

Deep modules!
</p>

<h3>Arguments</h3>
<p>
    If a function has more than one parameter, the parameters should be named, if the language allows.
Named and default arguments are one of my favorite language features, and one of the biggest features missing from Go.
</p>

